{"name":"Ecstatic Red","hex":"#aa1122","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ecstatic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Feeling or characterized by ecstasy.","Extremely happy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Transports of delight; words or actions performed in a state of ecstasy.","A person in a state of ecstasy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ecstatic"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ecstasy (emotion)","blocks":[{"text":"Ecstasy is a subjective experience of total involvement of the subject with an object of their awareness. In classical Greek literature, it refers to removal of the mind or body \"from its normal place of function.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Rom%2C_Santa_Maria_della_Vittoria%2C_Die_Verz%C3%BCckung_der_Heiligen_Theresa_%28Bernini%29.jpg/330px-Rom%2C_Santa_Maria_della_Vittoria%2C_Die_Verz%C3%BCckung_der_Heiligen_Theresa_%28Bernini%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecstasy_(emotion)"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-